{"generated":"2026-06-29T13:08:04.162860+00:00","period_start":"2026-06-22T17:21:00+00:00","period_end":"2026-06-29T11:21:00+00:00","snapshot_count":29,"html":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<style>\nbody { font-family: Georgia, serif; background: #f5ecd7; color: #1a1a1a; max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }\nh1 { text-align: center; font-size: 2.8em; letter-spacing: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; border-top: 6px double #1a1a1a; border-bottom: 6px double #1a1a1a; padding: 10px 0; margin-bottom: 4px; }\nh2 { text-align: center; font-size: 1em; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-top: 2px; margin-bottom: 16px; }\nh3 { font-size: 1.35em; text-transform: uppercase; border-bottom: 2px solid #1a1a1a; margin-top: 24px; }\np { line-height: 1.75; margin: 10px 0; text-align: justify; }\nblockquote { background: #e8d9b5; border: 3px double #1a1a1a; margin: 20px 0; padding: 16px 20px; font-style: italic; }\nblockquote strong { display: block; font-style: normal; font-size: 1.1em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding-bottom: 4px; }\nhr { border: none; border-top: 3px double #1a1a1a; margin: 28px 0; }\n.subhead { font-style: italic; font-size: 1.05em; display: block; margin-top: -6px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: #444; }\n.byline { font-size: 0.85em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: #555; margin-bottom: 16px; display: block; }\n.leaderboard { background: #1a1a1a; color: #f5ecd7; padding: 12px 18px; margin: 16px 0; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }\n.leaderboard strong { display: block; text-align: center; font-size: 1.1em; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #f5ecd7; padding-bottom: 4px; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<h1>The Vendetta Gazette</h1>\n<h2>Vol. XIII &bull; July 6, 2026 &bull; &ldquo;All the Blood That&rsquo;s Fit to Print&rdquo; &bull; Two Cents (If You&rsquo;re Still Alive to Pay)</h2>\n\n<div class=\"leaderboard\">\n<strong>&#9733; TERRITORY GAINS THIS WEEK &#9733;</strong>\nSir Caprice &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +160 turfs<br>\nFree Willy &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +15 turfs<br>\nDonald Trump &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +10 turfs<br>\nWu-Tang &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +9 turfs<br>\nFlattop &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +2 turfs<br>\nLucy's road &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +1 turfs\n</div>\n\n<h3>The Annihilator Ascendant — A City Devoured Whole</h3>\n<span class=\"subhead\">Sir Caprice Seizes One Hundred and Sixty Turfs, Smashes Thirty-Two Headquarters, and Apparently Has No Intention of Stopping Whatsoever</span>\n<span class=\"byline\">By Our Man in the Trenches, Ignatius P. Flambeau</span>\n\n<p>This correspondent confessed last week, with no small degree of theatrical exhaustion, that Sir Caprice had laid waste to ten enemy headquarters and claimed eighty-three turfs in a single seven-day span. He advised readers to brace themselves. Dear reader, you did not brace nearly enough.</p>\n\n<p>In the week ending this very edition, <strong>Sir Caprice — The Annihilator, the Unstoppable, the Scourge Made Flesh</strong> — has surpassed his own already-ludicrous benchmark by a margin that would make Julius Caesar blush and Napoleon weep into his bicorne. One hundred and sixty turfs seized. Thirty-two enemy headquarters stormed, looted, and left as smouldering monuments to the folly of resistance. Ninety-one raids conducted upon the trembling storehouses of his enemies. The man has not slept. He cannot possibly have slept. His garrison now stands at a mountainous <strong>6,965 gangsters</strong> — sixty more enrolled this week alone — a private army that dwarfs anything Vendetta City has witnessed in living memory.</p>\n\n<p>Among those who fell beneath The Annihilator's boot this week: <strong>Ehsan</strong>, <strong>Biggs</strong>, <strong>laeawolf</strong>, <strong>RadithJuno</strong> (struck twice, the poor wretch), <strong>Hiuu</strong> (also struck twice — one wonders if the man has a death wish or merely a very poor memory), and the numerical enigma known only as <strong>4542323412</strong>, whose headquarters presumably held some sentimental value it no longer possesses. Thirty-two souls in total kissed their command posts goodbye, scrambling to reconstitute their operations from whatever forgotten back-alley turf they still held in reserve.</p>\n\n<p>Two fortresses dared to hold firm against the onslaught — their garrisons numbering eleven or more stalwart defenders, forcing even The Annihilator's henchmen to fall back from the threshold. These \"HQ Destroyed\" engagements stand as the week's sole consolation prizes for a beleaguered citizenry. The walls held. The flags did not change. It was, by any measure, a moral victory of the most pyrrhic variety.</p>\n\n<hr>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"640\" height=\"220\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#0a0800;display:block;margin:18px auto\">\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" letter-spacing=\"2\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">TERRITORY GAINS THIS WEEK</text>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"620\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#3a2a00\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Sir Caprice</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"35\" width=\"400\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"566\" y=\"48\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+160</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Free Willy</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"63\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"203\" y=\"76\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+15</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Donald Trump</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"91\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"191\" y=\"104\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+10</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Wu-Tang</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"119\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"188\" y=\"132\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+9</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Flattop</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"147\" width=\"5\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"171\" y=\"160\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+2</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"188\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Lucy's road</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"175\" width=\"2\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"168\" y=\"188\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+1</text>\n</svg>\n\n\n<h3>The Fallen: Soprano, Duchess, and the Ruins of Former Greatness</h3>\n<span class=\"subhead\">Tony Soprano Loses Twenty-Seven Turfs and Is Raided Twenty-Three Times; Duchess Reduced to Zero Garrison</span>\n<span class=\"byline\">By Our City Desk Correspondent</span>\n\n<p>While the city's attention fixes upon The Annihilator's inexorable march, spare a moment's sympathy — or at minimum, a raised eyebrow — for those ground beneath the wheels of this terrible machine. <strong>Tony Soprano</strong>, the once-swaggering boss of the East Quarter, has suffered the indignity of losing twenty-seven turfs this week whilst being raided a staggering twenty-three times. His garrison, still a respectable 2,088 strong, suggests the man retains the capacity for a comeback — but his coffers have been picked cleaner than a Thanksgiving carcass on a Depression breadline.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Duchess</strong> fares considerably worse. Having shed twenty-three turfs and absorbed eighteen raids upon her remaining holdings, she arrives at week's end with a garrison of precisely <em>zero</em>. Not a henchman. Not a bouncer. Not so much as an elderly doorman with a hat pin. Whether her forces were destroyed in battle, recalled in panicked retreat, or have simply deserted en masse to seek more promising employment is a matter this newspaper's investigators are pursuing with characteristic tenacity.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Starseed</strong>, <strong>Ekmu</strong>, and <strong>Wcrypto</strong> round out the week's gallery of the aggr\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"640\" height=\"276\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#0a0800;display:block;margin:18px auto\">\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" letter-spacing=\"2\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">HEAVIEST LOSSES THIS WEEK</text>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"620\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#3a2a00\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Tony Soprano</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"35\" width=\"400\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"566\" y=\"48\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-27</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Duchess</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"63\" width=\"340\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"506\" y=\"76\" fill=\"#8b1a1a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">-23</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,se